James inquired about a new remote control that he expected to work as a drop-in replacement for his old one but found it non-functional. I clarified that off-brand or universal remotes often require additional setup steps to work with TVs. I suggested inserting fresh batteries, checking for a TV-specific code, and programming the remote either through direct code entry or an auto-search method. I emphasized the importance of following the instructions precisely and testing various functions to ensure compatibility. Lastly, I mentioned the possibility of checking the remote's compatibility with the TV model and offered further assistance if needed.
